@page "/gestures-renderer"

<PageTitle>Gestures × Renderer | The Singularity Workshop</PageTitle>

<main class="gesture-brief">
    <header class="brief-header">
        <a class="back-link" href="/hub">← RETURN TO THE HUB</a>
        <p class="eyebrow">WORKSHOP INTEGRATION BAY / CPU POSE → PRESENTATION</p>
        <h1>Gestures <span>×</span> Renderer</h1>
        <p class="intro">Inspect the current integration seam between authored procedures, evaluated local pose data, and observer-aware presentation. This is an architecture and evidence panel—not a live motion demo.</p>
        <div class="status-line" role="status">
            <span class="status-chip">INTEGRATION PLAN</span>
            <span>Runtime adapter not connected · No motion is being simulated here</span>
        </div>
    </header>

    <section class="pipeline" aria-labelledby="pipeline-title">
        <div class="section-heading">
            <p class="eyebrow">DATA FLOW / RESPONSIBILITY BOUNDARIES</p>
            <h2 id="pipeline-title">One pose. Several distinct responsibilities.</h2>
        </div>
        <ol class="flow-list">
            <li><span class="step">01</span><strong>Procedure definition</strong><p>Authored keyframes, named local transforms, duration, and caller-provided variation inputs.</p><small>Gestures model</small></li>
            <li class="flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</li>
            <li><span class="step">02</span><strong>CPU reference evaluation</strong><p>The evaluator samples a requested time and returns normalized progress, completion, local transforms, and root presentation offset.</p><small>Implemented on the referenced working branch</small></li>
            <li class="flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</li>
            <li><span class="step">03</span><strong>Consumer / rig adapter</strong><p>Must map names to real rig nodes, compose parent transforms, define coordinate conversion, and handle unmapped names.</p><small>Pending · not implemented by this page</small></li>
            <li class="flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</li>
            <li><span class="step">04</span><strong>Renderer representation</strong><p>Renderer currently builds frames from resolved draw commands; its public contract does not define a named skeleton or skeletal-pose input.</p><small>Pose interchange contract pending</small></li>
            <li class="flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</li>
            <li><span class="step">05</span><strong>Presentation backend</strong><p>Visualize/backend work may consume a future agreed representation after the seam and its costs are measured.</p><small>GPU parity unmeasured</small></li>
        </ol>
        <p class="figure-note">This is a static architecture diagram. It does not execute GestureEvaluator, animate a rig, produce RenderFrame data, or imply a working adapter.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="status-grid" aria-label="Integration maturity">
        <article class="status-card implemented">
            <p class="eyebrow">01 / CPU REFERENCE</p>
            <h2>Implemented on working branch</h2>
            <p>Engine-neutral definitions and evaluation are available for review. CI for Gestures PR #10 previously passed build, tests, and package-artifact creation; that is not GPU parity or physical validation.</p>
            <a href="https://github.com/TrentBest/TheSingularityWorkshop.Gestures/pull/10" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Review Gestures PR #10 ↗</a>
        </article>
        <article class="status-card pending">
            <p class="eyebrow">02 / RIG MAPPING</p>
            <h2>Pending</h2>
            <p>No agreed rig-node identity, hierarchy composition, coordinate convention, root-offset policy, or missing-name behavior is connected here.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="status-card pending">
            <p class="eyebrow">03 / RENDERER POSE CONTRACT</p>
            <h2>Pending</h2>
            <p>Do not treat a single draw command's world transform as a multi-node skeletal-pose API. A real adapter must target a supported representation.</p>
            <a href="https://github.com/TrentBest/TheSingularityWorkshop.Gestures/blob/work/planar-ik-reference/docs/RENDERER_POSE_HANDOFF_PROPOSAL.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read pose-handoff proposal ↗</a>
        </article>
        <article class="status-card external">
            <p class="eyebrow">04 / PHYSICAL EVIDENCE</p>
            <h2>Owned externally</h2>
            <p>Pose evaluation does not prove contact, grip, load-bearing support, collision outcomes, successful boarding, or any other domain success. Physics and the authoritative domain owner supply that evidence.</p>
        </article>
    </section>

    <section class="boundary-panel">
        <p class="eyebrow">THE EVIDENCE BOUNDARY</p>
        <h2>Evaluation completion is not physical success.</h2>
        <p><code>IsComplete</code> means the requested time-based evaluation reached its end. It does not mean a hand contacted a handhold, a foot landed safely, or a soldier boarded a vehicle. Rendering is presentation evidence, not authoritative world state.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="source-panel" aria-labelledby="source-title">
        <p class="eyebrow">SOURCE TRAIL / REVIEW THE REAL CONTRACTS</p>
        <h2 id="source-title">Follow the implementation, not an illustration.</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/TrentBest/TheSingularityWorkshop.Gestures/tree/work/planar-ik-reference" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Gestures working branch ↗</a> <span>Definition and CPU reference work; branch remains under review.</span></li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/TrentBest/TheSingularityWorkshop.Gestures/blob/development/docs/REQUESTS_AND_INTEGRATION.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Gestures integration contract ↗</a> <span>Package boundaries and responsibility direction.</span></li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/TrentBest/TheSingularityWorkshop.Gestures/blob/work/planar-ik-reference/tests/TheSingularityWorkshop.Gestures.Tests/GestureEvaluatorTests.cs" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CPU evaluator tests ↗</a> <span>Reference checks, not a physical simulation.</span></li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/TrentBest/TheSingularityWorkshop.Renderer" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Renderer repository ↗</a> <span>Observer-relative representation and render-frame construction.</span></li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <footer class="brief-footer">THE SINGULARITY WORKSHOP · INTEGRATION BAY · NO MOCK MOTION</footer>
</main>

